This mutation makes movement toward the goals respect nearby enemies. `progress` now penalises destination tiles within 2 of an enemy, and `score` scales the resulting gain by 10 so a move is worth taking only when it still closes distance on a safe tile. This costs one `enemies()` call per candidate move, so it is the fuel risk to watch.

```python
@gene("s4", "distance gained toward goals, minus a penalty for ending next to enemies", parents=["s4"])
def progress(t: Tile) -> Num:
    d = at(goal_field(), me().pos) - at(goal_field(), t)
    near = sum(1 for u in enemies() if dist(u.pos, t) <= 2)
    return 3 * d - 4 * near

@gene("s1", "value of doing this option now", parents=["s1"])
def score(o: Option) -> Num:
    if o.kind == PICK:
        return 1
    if o.kind == BUY:
        return 100 if o.item == 6 else 0
    if o.kind == RECALL:
        return 90 if me().health_frac < 0.35 else 0
    if o.kind == ATTACK:
        if o.unit.is_champion:
            return 80
        return 60 if gems() == 0 else 0
    if o.kind == TRIBUTE:
        return 70
    if o.kind == MOVE:
        p = progress(o.tile)
        return 10 * p if p > 0 else 0
    return 0
```

This mutation changes the MOVE branch of `score` and adds a danger penalty to `progress`. Moves toward goals keep their priority only when health is above 40%, and `progress` subtracts a penalty for enemy champions within 2 tiles of the target step, so the bot stops walking into fights it would lose.

```python
@gene("s4", "how much closer a step brings me to the goals, minus danger near the step", parents=["s4"])
def progress(t: Tile) -> Num:
    danger = count(1 for u in enemies() if u.is_champion and dist(u.pos, t) <= 2)
    return at(goal_field(), me().pos) - at(goal_field(), t) - 1.5 * danger


