```python
@gene("new", "value of casting an ability: damage/cc on champions or camps, heal/shield when hurt", parents=["s1"])
def cast_value(o: Option) -> Num:
    k = slot_kind(o.slot)
    if k == AB_HEAL or k == AB_SHIELD:
        return 75 if me().health_frac < 0.7 else 0
    if k == AB_DAMAGE or k == AB_AOE or k == AB_CC:
        if exists(o.unit):
            if o.unit.is_champion and o.unit.is_enemy:
                return 85
            if o.unit.is_camp and gems() == 0:
                return 65
        return 0
    return 0
```

The change makes `goal_field` route around walls and camp tiles, and bounds the search to a radius-3 window around me. `progress` only reads the field near my position, so the bounded search should give the same step choices at lower engine cost.

```python
@gene("s3", "distance field to the goals, routed around walls and camps, searched only near me", parents=["s3"])
def goal_field() -> Field:
    return field_avoid(goals(), walls() | camp_tiles(), near(me().pos, 3))
```

```python
@gene("s4", "how much closer a step brings me to the goals", parents=["s4"])
def progress(t: Tile) -> Num:
    return at(goal_field(), me().pos) - at(goal_field(), t)
